Advanced Troubleshooting Techniques
Creating a Comprehensive Diagnostic Script
Create a master diagnostic script that combines all troubleshooting checks:

sudo nano /usr/local/bin/ipa-full-diagnostic.sh
Add the following comprehensive script:

#!/bin/bash
# Comprehensive IPA Authentication Diagnostic Script

LOG_FILE="/tmp/ipa-diagnostic-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).log"

echo "=== IPA Authentication Diagnostic Report ===" | tee $LOG_FILE
echo "Generated on: $(date)" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo "Hostname: $(hostname)" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# System Information
echo "--- System Information ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
uname -a | tee -a $LOG_FILE
cat /etc/redhat-release | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# IPA Server Status
echo "--- IPA Server Status ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
sudo ipactl status | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# DNS Configuration
echo "--- DNS Configuration ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
cat /etc/resolv.conf | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# Kerberos Configuration
echo "--- Kerberos Configuration ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
sudo klist -k /etc/krb5.keytab | head -10 | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# Recent Authentication Failures
echo "--- Recent Authentication Failures ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
sudo grep -i "authentication failure" /var/log/secure | tail -5 | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# Certificate Status
echo "--- Certificate Status ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
sudo ipa-getcert list | grep -E "(Request ID|status|expires)" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

# Disk Space
echo "--- Disk Space ---" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
df -h | grep -E "(Filesystem|/var|/tmp)" | tee -a $LOG_FILE
echo | tee -a $LOG_FILE

echo "Diagnostic report saved to: $LOG_FILE"
Make it executable and run:

sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/ipa-full-diagnostic.sh
