Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Clock Skew Problems
Symptoms: Authentication fails with time-related errors

Solution:

# Synchronize time with NTP
sudo chrony makestep

# Verify time synchronization
sudo chrony sources -v

# Restart Kerberos services
sudo systemctl restart krb5kdc
Issue 2: LDAP Connection Failures
Symptoms: Cannot connect to LDAP directory

Solution:

# Check LDAP service status
sudo systemctl status dirsrv@EXAMPLE-COM

# Test LDAP connectivity
ldapsearch -x -H ldap://ipa.example.com -b "dc=example,dc=com" "(objectclass=*)" | head -20

# Restart directory service if needed
sudo systemctl restart dirsrv@EXAMPLE-COM
Issue 3: DNS Resolution Problems
Symptoms: Cannot resolve IdM server hostname

Solution:

# Add IdM server to /etc/hosts temporarily
echo "192.168.1.100 ipa.example.com" | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts

# Fix DNS configuration
sudo nmcli con mod "System eth0" ipv4.dns "192.168.1.100"
sudo nmcli con up "System eth0"
Preventive Measures
Setting Up Monitoring
Create a monitoring script for authentication health:
sudo nano /usr/local/bin/ipa-health-monitor.sh
#!/bin/bash
# IPA Health Monitoring Script

ALERT_EMAIL="admin@example.com"
LOG_FILE="/var/log/ipa-health.log"

# Check IPA services
if ! sudo ipactl status >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "$(date): IPA services are down" >> $LOG_FILE
    # Send alert (configure mail system as needed)
fi

# Check certificate expiration (30 days warning)
CERT_EXPIRY=$(sudo openssl x509 -in /var/lib/ipa/certs/httpd.crt -noout -dates | grep notAfter | cut -d= -f2)
EXPIRY_EPOCH=$(date -d "$CERT_EXPIRY" +%s)
CURRENT_EPOCH=$(date +%s)
DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRY=$(( (EXPIRY_EPOCH - CURRENT_EPOCH) / 86400 ))

if [ $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRY -lt 30 ]; then
    echo "$(date): Certificate expires in $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRY days" >> $LOG_FILE
fi

# Check disk space
DISK_USAGE=$(df /var | tail -1 | awk '{print $5}' | sed 's/%//')
if [ $DISK_USAGE -gt 80 ]; then
    echo "$(date): Disk usage is at ${DISK_USAGE}%" >> $LOG_FILE
fi
Set up a cron job for regular monitoring:
# Add to crontab
echo "0 */6 * * * /usr/local/bin/ipa-health-monitor.sh" | sudo crontab -
